{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevLcjEnNp3KFKhwM8Bjh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n```\n\n**Requirement, restated:**\nAdd a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that cancels active orders by changing their status to `CANCELLED`, prevents creation of shipments for cancelled orders, and follows all-or-nothing semantics with conflict avoidance for confirmed shipments.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n\n- Order model (`Order.kt:11`): Currently has no status field; needs `status: OrderStatus` added.\n- OrderRepository (`OrderRepository.kt`): In-memory store using ConcurrentHashMap; no status awareness yet.\n- OrderController (`OrderController.kt`): Creates orders, reads them, lists them. No cancel endpoint. When creating an order, needs to initialize status as `ACTIVE`.\n- Shipment model (`Shipment.kt:9`): Already has `status: ShipmentStatus` with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED.\n- ShipmentRepository (`ShipmentRepository.kt`): No method to find shipments by orderId; needs one added.\n- ShipmentController (`ShipmentController.kt:26`): Creates shipments without checking order status; needs to reject creation for `CANCELLED` orders with 409.\n- ApiExceptions (`ApiExceptions.kt`): Defines ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409), ValidationException (400).\n- ErrorCode enum (`ApiError.kt:31`): Currently has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED. Needs new codes for cancel-specific errors.\n- GlobalExceptionHandler (`GlobalExceptionHandler.kt`): Central exception handling; no changes needed.\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n\n- All errors use the ApiError envelope: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }`\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler catches them.\n- 404 = ResourceNotFoundException for missing resources\n- 409 = ConflictException for state/business conflicts\n- All tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions on both status and error envelope\n- Repositories are in-memory using ConcurrentHashMap\n- Tests reset repositories in @BeforeEach\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Must add `status: OrderStatus` field and create enum `OrderStatus { ACTIVE, CANCELLED }`\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** — Must add `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` and potentially update finding methods (no changes really needed, store already holds all orders)\n3. **OrderController.kt** — Must add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint; update create() to set status to ACTIVE\n4. **Shipment.kt** — No changes; already has status\n5. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Must add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method\n6. **ShipmentController.kt** — Must check in create() that order exists and is not CANCELLED; throw 409 if CANCELLED\n7. **ApiError.kt** — Must add error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` (or similar to indicate shipment creation rejected) and potentially `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` (for when CONFIRMED shipment blocks cancel)\n8. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Must add tests for cancel endpoint behavior\n9. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Must add test that creating shipment for cancelled order returns 409\n\n**Risks:**\n\n- The ShipmentController currently doesn't validate that the orderId exists; I need to inject OrderRepository to check this.\n- The cancel operation must be atomic: if any shipment is CONFIRMED, nothing changes. This is currently handled by throwing before any save.\n- Concurrent access: Both repositories use ConcurrentHashMap, so basic thread safety is present, but the cancel operation itself isn't transactional.\n- If a shipment is confirmed while cancel is in-flight, we might get a race condition. The ticket says \"all-or-nothing\", which I interpret as: check all shipments first, and if any is CONFIRMED, throw before touching anything.\n\n**Open questions:**\n\n1. When a shipment for a cancelled order is attempted, should the error code be `ORDER_CANCELLED` or should we use an existing code? The ticket doesn't specify, but says \"rejected with HTTP 409\" — I'll need a new error code like `ORDER_CANCELLED`.\n2. Should the cancel endpoint return the updated order in the response? The ticket says \"returns the order\" — yes, same as create endpoint.\n3. For finding shipments by orderId, should I add a method to ShipmentRepository or access the store directly in the controller? I'll add the method to keep concerns separated.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**\n   - Add `enum class OrderStatus { ACTIVE, CANCELLED }`\n   - Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class\n   - Keep CreateOrderRequest unchanged\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**\n   - Update `create()` to initialize new orders with `status = OrderStatus.ACTIVE`\n   - Add new `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n     - Finds the order; throws ResourceNotFoundException (404) if not found\n     - If order is already CANCELLED, return it as-is (idempotent)\n     - Check all shipments for this order; if any is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException (409) without modifying anything\n     - Set order status to CANCELLED, save it, cancel all CREATED shipments\n     - Return the cancelled order with HTTP 200\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt**\n   - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String)`: This is just an alias to findById, but keeping the same name as for shipments for consistency. Actually, we already have findById, so no new method needed here.\n   - Add `update(order: Order): Order` to explicitly handle updates (or reuse save() which already does this)\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt**\n   - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to find all shipments for an order\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**\n   - Inject OrderRepository\n   - In create(), check:\n     - Order exists: if not, let it proceed (ticket says \"keeps current behaviour\")\n     - Order is not CANCELLED: if CANCELLED, throw ConflictException (409) with new error code\n\n6. **ApiError.kt**\n   - Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code (for shipment creation rejection)\n   - Add `ORDER_SHIPMENT_CONFLICT` or similar (for when cancel is blocked by confirmed shipment)\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**\n   - Test: Cancel an active order successfully → 200, order status is CANCELLED\n   - Test: Cancel an already-cancelled order → 200, status still CANCELLED (idempotent)\n   - Test: Cancel an order with a CONFIRMED shipment → 409, order stays ACTIVE\n   - Test: Cancel a non-existent order → 404\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**\n   - Test: Create shipment for a cancelled order → 409\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\n- **Soft-delete vs status field**: I considered marking orders as deleted instead of using a status enum. Rejected because:\n  - The ticket explicitly says \"a status\" and lists \"ACTIVE\" and \"CANCELLED\" as states\n  - Status is more explicit and matches the pattern already used by Shipment\n  - Soft-delete would still require similar checks\n\n- **Optimistic locking**: I considered using a version field for concurrent updates. Rejected because:\n  - The ticket doesn't mention it\n  - In-memory store with ConcurrentHashMap doesn't need it\n  - The existing codebase doesn't use it\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. Controller finds order; throws 404 if not found\n3. Check all shipments: if any CONFIRMED, throw 409 (ORDER_SHIPMENT_CONFLICT) without saving\n4. Set order.status = CANCELLED, repository saves\n5. For each CREATED shipment: set status = CANCELLED, repository saves\n6. Return order (200 OK)\n\n*Cancel already-CANCELLED order:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. Controller finds order\n3. Order status is already CANCELLED\n4. Return it as-is (200 OK)\n\n*Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. Controller finds order\n3. Find all shipments for order\n4. Detect CONFIRMED shipment\n5. Throw ConflictException (409, ORDER_SHIPMENT_CONFLICT)\n6. No database changes\n\n*Create shipment for CANCELLED order:*\n1. POST /shipments\n2. ShipmentController calls create()\n3. Check if order exists (keep current behaviour if not)\n4. Check if order is CANCELLED\n5. If CANCELLED, throw ConflictException (409, ORDER_CANCELLED)\n6. If not CANCELLED, proceed normally\n\n*Unknown order:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. Controller calls repository.findById()\n3. Returns null\n4. Throw ResourceNotFoundException (404, ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest** (new tests):\n   - `cancelsActiveOrder()`: Create O-1, cancel it, verify status is CANCELLED and shipment is cancelled\n   - `cancelCancelledOrderIsIdempotent()`: Create O-2, cancel twice, both return 200\n   - `cancelOrderWithConfirmedShipmentReturns409()`: Create O-3, create CONFIRMED shipment, attempt cancel, verify 409 and order still ACTIVE\n   - `cancelNonExistentOrderReturns404()`: Attempt to cancel O-missing, verify 404\n\n2. **ShipmentControllerTest** (new test):\n   - `createShipmentForCancelledOrderReturns409()`: Create O-4, cancel it, attempt to create shipment, verify 409\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":269,"cache_read_input_tokens":18558,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":269},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa5d94d2-9155-4ab9-8181-60cdec7ca5bd","uuid":"4902887c-de1c-4c21-a9ee-beef4c40a687","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:50:09.280Z","request_id":"req_011CevLcih3XuvBomYvRg91L"}
